      "clause": "#542 \u00a73 Correlation: raw commands keep one unacknowledged candidate per target and never use FIFO or recency for ACK/error ownership; named sockets are exact, while compatible inquiries may use their per-target FIFO only when no command candidate collides.",
      "rationale": "1.x temporal command fallback is intentionally rejected because raw VISCA carries no request identity. The v2 production engine serializes only the pre-ACK raw window, restores socket concurrency after ACK, ignores ambiguous collisions, and retains FIFO solely for compatible inquiry replies."
    },
